1209 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Jungle Orcs are a unique breed of orc native to the thick\054 ancient canopies of places like Amobo\054 Corrow\054 and the Wild Hook\056 Standing noticeably shorter than their massive Pliaran kin\054 these tree\055dwelling nomads average around five feet tall and feature elongated arms designed for moving effortlessly through the branches\056 Their hunched posture and heavy\054 calloused knuckles allow them to move swiftly along both the forest floor and the highest limbs\054 making them exceptional climbers and trackers\056\n\nDespite their intimidating physical presence\054 complete with long faces\054 snout\055like features\054 and upward\055curving tusks\054 Jungle Orcs reject the brutal reputation usually attached to their kind\056 They build elaborate arboreal civilizations high above the ground and act as dedicated caretakers of the wilderness\056 Driven by a desire for harmony rather than conflict\054 their communities value quiet\054 steady coexistence with the natural world over conquest or bloodshed\056\n\nTheir culture revolves around protection\054 craftsmanship\054 and a deep understanding of the environment\056 Utilizing light weapons like scimitars alongside traditional clubs\054 Jungle Orcs navigate the dense foliage with unmatched agility and grace\056 Whether tending to the canopy or trading goods across their forest territories\054 they remain one of the most peaceful and adaptable societies in the realm\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 1210 0 R
     /Pg 1202 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

