1227 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Orcs of Pliara differ wildly from one another in both appearance and behavior\056 While many orcs live up to the stereotype of aggression\054 anger\054 and chaos\054 many others live very different lives\056 Some Orcs are shepherds of the wild\054 traveling around in a nomadic pursuit\056\n\nOther Orcs build colonies in the trees and live among the wilds of the jungle\056 Regardless of behavior or appearance\054 all orcs in Pliara share a similar ancestry and\054 as such\054 have very defining characteristics\056\n\nTheir faces are long with large\054 under\055developed noses\056 In some cases\054 Orcs lack nostrils completely\054 giving them a snout\055like appearance\056 Averaging between 6\0476\042 and 7\0476\042 with powerful builds and gray\054 brown\054 or green\055tinted skin\054 Orcs are monstrous creatures\056 Their canine teeth often protrude from their mouths as tusks\054 pointing upwards towards their large\054 oversized eyebrows\056 While most Orcs won\047t be found studying a book\054 they often excel in tasks requiring brute strength\056\n\nAlthough Jungle Orcs and Plains Orcs frequently do not meet the stereotypes set before them by the savage Pliaran Orcs\054 most other races fear all Orcs\056 The brutal savagery of Pliaran Orcs has spun tales\054 fact and fiction\054 throughout all of Pliara\056 Many Elven children are told bedtime stories of being taken by Orcs and turned into slaves if they misbehaved\054 forced to work alongside the Humans\056 These stereotypes and prejudices make it difficult for even the nicest of Plains or Jungle Orc to become trusted in a new place\054 even as a merchant or tradesman\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 1228 0 R
     /Pg 1204 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

